What we use from Slidev:

- The published npm package `@slidev/parser` (MIT) splits slides.md into slides and
  reads frontmatter and notes. It is a dependency, not copied code.
- The click logic in src/app/lib/clicks.ts, v-click.ts and v-clicks.ts is a port of
  Slidev's packages/client/composables/useClicks.ts and its v-click / v-after / v-clicks
  modules, rewritten for Angular.
- The layout names, structure and styles (src/app/layouts and src/styles/layouts.css, from Slidev's
  client layouts and default theme), the first-slide-is-cover rule, the 16:9 canvas scaling formula and the
  click CSS classes follow Slidev's design.
- The navigation bar, context menu, overview, goto box, keyboard shortcuts, table of contents, slide transitions
  and the small built-in components (src/app/ui, lib/shortcuts.ts, lib/toc-tree.ts, lib/transitions.ts, builtin/,
  lib/v-switch.ts, lib/v-click-gap.ts) are ports of the matching Slidev client code, rewritten for Angular.

- The themes in themes/ (seriph, shibainu, bricks, apple-basic) rebuild the official Slidev themes (https://github.com/slidevjs/themes),
  which are licensed under the MIT License:

    Copyright (c) 2021 Slidev.js Team

  Original designs: seriph by Anthony Fu, shibainu and bricks by iiiiiiinès, apple-basic by Jeremy Meissner. The layout names and slots, CSS values,
  font settings and the eleven polygon shapes of bricks are ported to Angular; the components are new code. `theme: default` is the built-in look
  (see above). The images and other assets of those themes are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial): none of them was copied or embedded.
  Where an original draws a picture, the port uses its own CSS gradients. Each theme folder has a README that credits its author.

